stage: 1
finding: The candidate-input guard's exclusions do not match the extension package inputs. `isCandidateBuildInput()` ignores `.cache`, `.artifacts`, and `target` for both demos and extensions, but only demo copies use that predicate as their copy filter. Extensions are packed by `bun pm pack`, which does not apply the predicate and can include those paths. I reproduced this in an isolated temporary repo: `candidateInputChanges()` returned `[]` with an untracked `packages/ext/.cache/payload.js`, while `bun pm pack` included `package/.cache/payload.js` in the tarball. Thus a supported candidate with a workspace extension can pack locally generated content that differs from the pinned SHA without refusal, undermining build/source-map identity; test coverage for generated exclusions checks extension `node_modules`, not these packable paths. Align the guard with actual pack contents or exclude those paths from the package artifact. The corrected actual first-person candidate has no workspace extension, so this gap is not evidence that its regenerated artifact is wrong; it leaves the extension-input class unguarded.
